description: Core project conventions for PA Command Center
alwaysApply: true
---

This is Simon Ince's personal dashboard project. Read `/AGENTS.md` and
`/README.md` at the repo root first — they contain the full architecture,
panel contracts, and working conventions and are kept current.

Quick rules that matter most when editing:

- Verify every change against real, live data (real Gmail/Calendar/
  TickTick/triage-snapshot output via `curl http://localhost:8420/api/state`
  after `docker compose up -d --build`). Never claim something works from
  reading code alone.
- Each data source (Gmail, Calendar, TickTick, triage snapshot) must
  degrade independently to a clean "unavailable" state on error — never
  let one failing source crash or blank the whole dashboard.
- No frontend build step. `backend/static/` is plain HTML/CSS/vanilla JS
  served directly by FastAPI — don't introduce React/Vite/npm without
  explicit sign-off from Simon.
- Credentials are read-only Docker bind mounts from paths in `.env`
  (git-ignored). Never hardcode a token/secret in source, never commit
  `.env`, never touch anything under `.hermes/` from this repo.
- Visual style is currently Swiss International (see README "v5"
  section for the exact tokens) but has changed completely several times
  already at Simon's direction — keep styling in `style.css` decoupled
  from `state.py`/`main.py` data logic so restyles never require backend
  changes.
